  // doc: implicit step of +1) as a finite sequence of integers. The sequence
  // doc: contains start, start+1, ..., stop-1 in that order. If start >= stop
  // doc: the sequence is empty. Iteration over range(start, stop) yields these
  // doc: elements in increasing order. In Python this range object is lazy and
  // doc: immutable; here we return an explicit seq<int> with the same element
  // doc: order and content. No exception is raised for any integer start/stop.
