// doc: - This encodes Python's "last occurrence wins" rule for duplicate keys in a dict literal.
// doc: - This function is left as an abstract (uninterpreted) function in this theory; it is a pure
// doc:   mathematical mapping from an input seq of pairs to an output seq of pairs satisfying the above properties.
function DedupPairs<K, V>(pairs: seq<(K, V)>): seq<(K, V)>

